use std
into relax.amni

```amni
import os;
import math;
import binary;
import json;
import bake;
import gfx;
import gfx.linalg;
import gfx.gltf;
import gfx.motion;
import gfx.scene3d;
import clips;
import mix;
```

Byte helpers over a file buffer. `rx_u16(b const byte[:], at int) int` and `rx_u32(b const byte[:], at int) int` read little-endian unsigned values; `rx_f32(b const byte[:], at int) f32` is `binary::f32_from_bits(rx_u32(b, at) as u32)`. `rx_w16(b byte[>..]&, at int, v int)` stores the low two bytes of v little-endian at `b[at]` and `b[at + 1]`; `rx_w32(b byte[>..]&, at int, v int)` stores four bytes the same way.

`rx_acc(d json::Doc&, root int, ai int) int, int, int, int` returns the byte offset inside the binary chunk, the count, the component type and the byte stride of accessor ai: the accessor is element ai of the root's "accessors", its view is element `bk_int(d, bk_mem(d, ac, "bufferView"), 0)` of "bufferViews", the offset is the view's "byteOffset" plus the accessor's "byteOffset" (each `bk_int(..., 0)`), and the stride is the view's "byteStride" (default 0). `bk_mem(d, n, key)` returns the member node or -1 and `bk_int(d, n, dflt)` reads an integer node or returns dflt for -1; both come from bake.

Vertex store (globals). `P float3[>..]` rest positions; `VM int[>..]` which mesh argument each vertex came from; `J int[>..]` and `W f32[>..]` four joints and four weights per vertex; `JO int[>..]`, `JC int[>..]`, `WO int[>..]` and `WC int[>..]` per vertex: the absolute file offset of its joint quad, the joint component type, the absolute file offset of its weight quad and the weight component type; `EA int[>..]`, `EB int[>..]` and `EK int[>..]` the edge list and each edge's kind (0 a mesh edge, 1 a seam weld, 2 a cross-mesh link); `TR int[>..]` three vertex ids per triangle; `RO int[>..]` and `RC int[>..]` compressed neighbor rows; `G int[>..]` the loaded-asset vertex id of each vertex. A source store for weight transfer: `SP float3[>..]`, `SJ int[>..]` and `SW f32[>..]` (positions, four joints and four weights per source vertex).

`rx_wsize(ct int) int` is the byte size of one component: 1 for 5121, 2 for 5123, else 4.

`rx_gather(d json::Doc&, root int, buf const byte[:], b0 int, name const byte[:], mi int, src bool) int` adds every primitive of the node called name and returns how many vertices it added (0 and a printed "no mesh " plus the name when no node of that name has a "mesh"). Find the node by walking the root's "nodes" with `json::each`, comparing `json::as_string` of its "name" member, and take its "mesh" index; the mesh is that element of "meshes". For each element pr of the mesh's "primitives", with `at = bk_mem(d, pr, "attributes")`: read the POSITION, JOINTS_0 and WEIGHTS_0 accessors (their indices are `bk_int(d, bk_mem(d, at, key), -1)`; skip the primitive when any is negative) and the "indices" accessor. Let base be `P.len`. For each vertex v below the position count: the position is three f32 at `b0 + po + (ps if ps > 0 else 12) * v`; the joint quad starts at `b0 + jo + (js if js > 0 else 4 * rx_wsize(jct)) * v` and each joint k is the u8 or u16 at that start plus k times its size; the weight quad starts at `b0 + wo + (ws if ws > 0 else 4 * rx_wsize(wct)) * v`, and weight k is an f32 for 5126, the u8 divided by 255.0 for 5121 and the u16 divided by 65535.0 for 5123. When src is true push only the position onto SP, the joints onto SJ and the weights onto SW and add no edges. Otherwise push the position, mi, the joints, the weights, both starts and both component types, and then for each triangle t below index count / 3 read the three indices (u16 for 5123, u32 for 5125, u8 otherwise) at `b0 + io + size * i` push base + i0, base + i1 and base + i2 onto TR and the three edges (base + i0, base + i1), (base + i1, base + i2), (base + i2, base + i0) onto EA and EB, each with kind 0 on EK.

`rx_link(weld f32, reach f32) int, int` adds edges between vertices that should move together and returns the counts of weld links and cross-mesh links. Hash every vertex into a grid of 0.02-meter cells (a cell key from the floored coordinates, stored as sorted pairs of key and vertex, or as per-cell lists; any correct spatial hash). For each vertex v look at the 27 neighboring cells: every other vertex u with u > v closer than weld becomes an edge of kind 1 (a seam weld). Separately keep the nearest vertex u of a different mesh (VM differs) closer than reach and, when one exists, add the edge (v, u) with kind 2.

`rx_mask(v int, lo f32, hi f32) f32` keeps the hands out of the hip band: it is the product of two ramps, the height ramp (1 when lo <= P[v].y <= hi, falling linearly to 0 over 0.03 m outside) and the side ramp (1 when `abs(P[v].x) <= 0.24`, falling linearly to 0 by 0.27).

`rx_transfer(lo f32, hi f32) int` copies weights from the source store and returns how many vertices took them. Hash the source positions into 0.02-meter cells. For each vertex v with mask m = rx_mask(v, lo, hi) > 0, find the nearest source vertex by searching the cells within one cell of v, widening to two and then three cells when none is found; skip v when none is found within three cells. Accumulate into a dense array of 256 sums (with a touched list to clear) its own four weights times `1 - m` and the source vertex's four weights times m, keep the four largest sums (ties by lower joint), divide them by their total and store them as the vertex's joints and weights.

`rx_rows(cross bool)` rebuilds RO (P.len + 1 offsets) and RC from every edge in both directions, skipping kind-2 edges unless cross is true.

`rx_smooth(src const float3[:], out float3[>..]&, n int)` sets out to a copy of src and then n times replaces every vertex that has neighbors with half its own point plus half the mean of its neighbors' points, computed from the previous round (RO and RC as built).

`rx_frames(s const float3[:], fn float3[>..]&, ft float3[>..]&, fb float3[>..]&)` builds a frame per vertex over the points s. Normals: zero vectors, then for every triangle in TR add `linalg::cross(s[b] - s[a], s[c] - s[a])` to its three corners, then `linalg::unit3` each (float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 } when the length is below 1.0e-12). Tangent: the first neighbor u in RC (rows RO) whose edge `e = s[u] - s[v]` minus its normal part `n * linalg::dot3(e, n)` is longer than 1.0e-9, normalized; when none, `linalg::unit3(linalg::cross(n, float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }))`, or with float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 } when that is too short. Bitangent `linalg::cross(n, t)`.

`rx_lbs_from(src const float3[:], pm const gfx::mat4[:], out float3[>..]&)` resizes out to P.len and sets each vertex v to the linear-blend skinned point of src[v]: the sum over its four slots with weight w = W[4v + k] > 0 (and joint j = J[4v + k] with 0 <= j < pm.len) of `linalg::point(pm[j], src[v]) * w`. `rx_lbs(pm const gfx::mat4[:], out float3[>..]&)` calls `rx_lbs_from(P[..], pm, out)`.

`rx_mush(glb const byte[:], lib const byte[:], lo f32, hi f32, n int) int` bakes Delta Mush into the weights of the masked vertices and returns how many it changed. `let asset, it, sk, nlib = rx_scene(glb, lib)`; return 0 when asset < 0. Call `rx_rows(false)`. Rest: `rx_smooth(P[..], s0, n)`, `rx_frames(s0[..], ...)` and per vertex the delta `d = float3 { dot3(P[v] - s0[v], t), dot3(P[v] - s0[v], b), dot3(P[v] - s0[v], nrm) }`; mask `m[v] = rx_mask(v, lo, hi)`. Poses: for i below 20, `let c = rx_pose(i, nlib)`, skipping i when c < -1, and capture each. For every pose: `s3d::pose(it)`, `motion::joints(sk, pal)`, append pal to a pose-major `pm gfx::mat4[>..]` (jc = pal.len joints per pose), `rx_lbs(pal[..], l)`, `rx_smooth(l[..], s, n)`, `rx_frames(s[..], ...)`, and for every vertex the target `x = l[v] + (s[v] + t * d.x + b * d.y + nrm * d.z - l[v]) * m[v]` appended to a pose-major `xt float3[>..]`; add `|l[v] - x|^2` of masked vertices to e0. Solve each masked vertex v: candidates are the joints with weight > 0 of v and of its neighbors, ranked by summed weight (dense 256 sums with a touched list), at most 8, ties by lower joint. For pose p and candidate j let `a = linalg::point(pm[p * jc + j], P[v]) - xt[p * nv + v]`; build the K by K matrix `A[j][k] = sum over poses of dot3(a_j, a_k)` in a local f64 array, add `mu = 0.01 * trace(A) / K + 1.0e-12` to its diagonal and let `bv[j] = mu * w0[j]` where w0[j] is v's current weight for candidate j (0 when not among its own). Minimize `0.5 * w' A w - bv' w` over the simplex (w >= 0, sum 1) by 400 steps of projected gradient from w0 with step `1 / (max over rows of the sum of |A[j][k]|)`; project with the sort-based simplex projection (sort descending, find the largest r with `u[r] - (sum of the first r + 1 values - 1) / (r + 1) > 0`, subtract that threshold, clamp at 0). Keep the four largest, renormalize, and store them as v's joints and weights (unused slots joint 0 weight 0). Then two passes over kind-1 edges whose ends are both masked: give both ends the top four of the average of their two weight sets, renormalized. Finally recompute every pose with `rx_lbs` from the stored pm rows and add `|new - x|^2` of masked vertices to e1. Fold counts: a triangle of TR whose three corners all have mask >= 0.5 is folded in a pose when `dot3(cross(q[b] - q[a], q[c] - q[a]), r)` < 0, where q is the point set being checked and the reference r is the sum over its three corners of the skinned rest normal (with rest point p = P[v] and rest normal `nv = float3 { gltf::verts[G[v] * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 3], gltf::verts[G[v] * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 4], gltf::verts[G[v] * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 5] }`, add `(linalg::point(mm, p + nv) - linalg::point(mm, p)) * w` over the vertex's ORIGINAL four influences, which must be copied before the solve). Keep three totals over all poses: folds of the original skinning l, of the targets x and of the new skinning; and the same three for the last pose alone. Print "mush: ", the pose count, " poses, ", the masked count, " masked, rms to target ", `sqrt(e0 / (poses * masked)) * 1000.0`, " mm before, ", the same for e1, " mm after", then "mush folds (all poses): ", the three totals joined by " -> ", " | last pose: ", the three last-pose counts joined by " -> ". Return the masked count.

`rx_relax(lo f32, hi f32, iters int, a f32) int` smooths the weights and returns the number of vertices it moves; the mask of vertex v is rx_mask(v, lo, hi). Call `rx_rows(true)` and use RO and RC as the neighbor lists. Each iteration works from a copy of J and W: for a vertex with mask m > 0 and at least one neighbor, accumulate into a dense array of 256 sums (indexed by joint, with a list of touched joints to clear) its own four weights times `1 - a * m` and every neighbor's four weights times `a * m / degree`; keep the four largest sums (ties by lower joint), divide them by their total and write them back as the vertex's joints and weights (unused slots get joint 0 and weight 0). Vertices with mask 0 keep their values.

`rx_store(buf byte[>..]&)` writes every vertex back in place. Joints are written as u8 or u16 by JC. Weights for 5126 are written as f32 bits with `rx_w32(buf, at, binary::f32_bits(w) as int)`; for 5121 and 5123 the four weights are scaled to 255 or 65535, rounded, and the rounding difference from the full scale is added to the largest one so the four always sum to exactly 255 or 65535, then written as u8 or u16.

`main()`. With `a = args()`: when `a.len < 7` print "usage: relax <in.glb> <out.glb> <y low> <y high> <iterations> <mesh> [mesh ...] [from=<body.glb>] [mush=<clips.gltf>] [psd=<clips.gltf>]; smooths skin weights of the named meshes inside the height band, welded across seams and linked across meshes; from= first copies weights from the nearest vertex of that file's full skin; mush= then bakes Delta Mush over that clip library's poses into the band's weights; psd= builds hip pose-space corrective morph targets on the named meshes" and return. Read a[1] into a `byte[>..]` (print "no " and the path on failure). The JSON chunk length is `rx_u32(buf[..], 12)`; parse `buf[20..20 + jl]` with `json::parse` into a `json::Doc` (print "bad json: " plus the error and return on failure); `b0 = 20 + jl + 8`. For each argument k from 6 on that starts with none of "from=", "mush=" and "psd=", `rx_gather(doc, root, buf[..], b0, a[k], k - 6, false)` and print the mesh name and its vertex count. When an argument starts with "from=", read the file named by the rest of it into a second buffer, parse its JSON chunk the same way into a second `json::Doc`, call `rx_gather` on it for the mesh "skin" with src true, and print "source skin " and the source vertex count. Call `rx_link(0.0005, 0.015)`; when the source store is not empty call `rx_transfer(lo, hi)` and print "transferred " and its result; then call `rx_relax(lo, hi, iters, 0.5)` with lo, hi and iters parsed from a[3], a[4] and a[5]. When an argument starts with "mush=", call `rx_mush(a[1], the rest of it, lo, hi, 10)`. Call `rx_store(buf)`. When an argument starts with "psd=", call `rx_psd(a[1], the rest of it, lo, hi)` and, when it returns more than 0, `rx_write(doc, root, buf[..], a[2])`; otherwise write the buffer to a[2] with `write_file`. Print "relax: ", the vertex total, " vertices, ", the number moved, " moved, ", the edge count, " edges, ", the weld count, " welds, ", the cross-mesh count, " cross-mesh links -> " and a[2].

Pose helpers shared by the bakes. Module vars `var rx_pc = -1` (clip now playing for rx_pose) and `var rx_pt = 0.0` (its time, f32). `rx_scene(glb const byte[:], lib const byte[:]) int, int, int, int` loads the scene and returns the asset, the scene item, the skin index of the first named mesh and the number of library clips, or -1 for all four on failure. `let asset = gltf::load(glb)` (print "load fail" and fail when negative); `let it = s3d::add(asset)`; `let nlib = clips::clips_load(lib, asset)`; build the slot table exactly so: `var sl i32[22]; let first = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first; for i in 22 { sl[i] = if clips::kc_slot[i] < 0 { -1 } else { (clips::kc_slot[i] as int - first) as i32 }; }`, then call the unqualified `mix_open(asset, it, sl[..])` and for c in nlib the unqualified `mix_clip(clips::kc_nf[c], clips::kc_loop[c], clips::clips_frames(c))`; set `rx_pc = -1`. Map vertices: clear G; for every argument of `args()` from index 6 on that starts with none of "from=", "mush=" and "psd=", `let nd = gltf::find_node(asset, arg)` (skip when negative), remember `sk = gltf::nodes[nd].skin` from the first one, and for each primitive pr of `gltf::meshes[gltf::nodes[nd].mesh]` (`gltf::prims[ms.prims.first + pi]`) push `pr.vfirst + v` onto G for v in pr.vcount. When G.len differs from P.len print "vertex map mismatch ", G.len, " ", P.len and fail.

`rx_pose(i int, nlib int) int` sets the mixer to sample pose i of 20 and returns which clip group it came from: -1 for the bind pose (i == 0: call `mix_rest()`, set `rx_pc = -1`), 0..3 for a clip pose, -2 past the end or when the clip is missing. Poses 1..19 in order are clip group 0 "Idle_Loop" at times 0.5, 1.0, 1.5; group 1 "Walk_Formal_Loop" at 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0; group 2 "Dance_Loop" at 0.35, 0.7, 1.05, 1.4, 1.75, 2.1, 2.45, 2.8; group 3 "Sitting_Idle_Loop" at 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0 (group names from `rx_clipname(group)`). Find the library clip whose `clips::clips_name(c, buf)` equals the name (print "no clip " plus the name and return -2 when none). When it differs from rx_pc: `mix_play(c, 0.0)`, `rx_pc = c`, `rx_pt = 0.0`. Then while `rx_pt + 0.0001 < target` call `mix_advance(1.0 / 60.0)` and add 1.0 / 60.0 to rx_pt. Return the group.

`rx_polar(c0 float3, c1 float3, c2 float3, q0 linalg::Quat) linalg::Quat` returns the rotation nearest to the 3 by 3 matrix whose columns are c0, c1 and c2, by the iterative method of Mueller, Bender, Chentanez and Macklin (2016) warm-started at q0: up to 24 times, with r0, r1 and r2 the images of the unit axes under q (`linalg::qrotate`), `om = (cross3(r0, c0) + cross3(r1, c1) + cross3(r2, c2)) * (1 / (abs(dot3(r0, c0) + dot3(r1, c1) + dot3(r2, c2)) + 1.0e-9))`; with `w = length3(om)` stop when w < 1.0e-9, else `q = linalg::qnorm(linalg::qmul(linalg::qaxis(om * (1 / w), w), q))`. Return q.

`rx_arap(l const float3[:], lam const f32[:], fr const bool[:], x float3[>..]&, iters int)` solves as-rigid-as-possible targets (Sorkine and Alexa 2007) over the rows RO and RC as built: x starts as a copy of l and only vertices with fr[v] true move. Edge weight `rx_ew(a, b)`: 20.0 when `rx_d2(P[a], P[b]) < 0.0005 * 0.0005` (a seam weld), else 1.0. The rest edge of v to u is `e = P[v] - P[u]`. Per-vertex rotations `R linalg::Quat[>..]` start at the identity. Repeat iters times: local step, for every vertex v with a neighbor, columns `c0`, `c1` and `c2` are the sums over neighbors u of `(x[v] - x[u]) * (w * e.x)`, `* (w * e.y)` and `* (w * e.z)`, and `R[v] = rx_polar(c0, c1, c2, R[v])`; global step, conjugate gradients for up to 60 iterations over the free vertices, solving `(sum of w over all neighbors + lam[v]) * x[v] - (sum over free neighbors u of w * x[u]) = b[v]` with `b[v] = sum over neighbors u of w * 0.5 * (qrotate(R[v], e) + qrotate(R[u], e)) + lam[v] * l[v] + sum over fixed neighbors u of w * x[u]`. Run the three coordinates as independent systems in real arithmetic (residual, direction and the rr, alpha and beta scalars per coordinate), warm-started from the current x, and stop early once each coordinate's rr is below 1.0e-14.

Corrective store: module vars `var DP float3[>..]` and `var DN float3[>..]` (position and normal deltas in rest space, P.len entries per target, target-major), `var TK int[>..]` (driving slot), `var TF f32[>..]` and `var TB f32[>..]` (flex and abduction, degrees). `rx_blend(pal const gfx::mat4[:], v int) gfx::mat4` is the weight-blended skinning matrix of vertex v (`gfx::mat4` is a struct of four float4 columns c0, c1, c2 and c3): start from four zero float4 columns and add each of `pal[J[4v + k]]`'s columns `.c0`, `.c1`, `.c2` and `.c3` times w for its slots with weight w = W[4v + k] > 0 (and 0 <= joint < pal.len). `rx_grow(m bool[>..]&, n int)` marks, n times, every neighbor (rows RO and RC) of a vertex marked before that round.

`rx_psd(glb const byte[:], lib const byte[:], lo f32, hi f32) int` builds hip pose-space correctives and returns how many targets it made. `let asset, it, sk, nlib = rx_scene(glb, lib)`; return 0 when asset < 0. Call `rx_rows(true)` (cross-mesh links tie the garments to the skin), `psd_basis()`, and clear DP, DN, TK, TF and TB. Copy J and W into OJ and OW; `MK[v] = rx_mask(v, lo, hi)`. Soft vertices: `sf[v]` true when 1 minus the largest of its four weights exceeds 0.02, then `rx_grow(sf, 3)`. For each side slot k in [14, 18] with `slot_node[k] >= 0` (side name "L" for 14, "R" for 18) and each sample (f, b) in degrees of (45, 0), (90, 0), (120, 0), (-30, 0), (0, 45), (90, 30), in that order: `mix_rest()`, `mix_set(k, mix_swing(k, psd_dir(f, b)))`, `push()`, `s3d::pose(it)`, clear pal then `motion::joints(sk, pal)`, `rx_lbs(pal[..], l)`. Free set: `fr[v] = rx_d2(l[v], P[v]) > 1.0e-8`, then `rx_grow(fr, 4)`; `lam[v]` is 0.05 when sf[v] else 2.0. `rx_arap(l[..], lam[..], fr[..], x, 40)`. Vertex normals of l and of x: `rx_frames(l[..], nl, t1, b1)` and `rx_frames(x[..], nx, t2, b2)`. For each vertex v: when `rx_d2(x[v], l[v]) <= 1.0e-12` push zero deltas; else `B = rx_blend(pal[..], v)`, `Bi = linalg::inverse(B)`, push `linalg::direction(Bi, x[v] - l[v])` onto DP; the rest normal nr is the three floats at `G[v] * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 3`; `np = unit3(direction(B, nr))`; when `dot3(nl[v], nx[v]) < 0.999999`, rotate np by `qaxis(unit3(cross3(nl[v], nx[v])), acos(clamp(dot3(nl[v], nx[v]), -1.0, 1.0)))`; push `unit3(direction(Bi, np)) - nr` onto DN. Push k, f and b onto TK, TF and TB and call `mix_psd_add(-1, TK.len - 1, k, psd_dir(f, b))`. Print "psd ", the side name, " ", f, " ", b, ": ", the free count, " free, ", the count of nonzero deltas, " moved, max ", the largest delta length times 1000, " mm at ", the rest point P of that largest-delta vertex (x, y, z), " (", the counts of deltas longer than 5 mm and longer than 20 mm joined by " / ", "), folds ", `rx_folds(l[..], pal[..], OJ[..], OW[..], MK[..])`, " -> ", the same for x. After all samples call `mix_psd_ready()`. Then measure: for i below 20, `c = rx_pose(i, nlib)` (skip when c < -1), `s3d::pose(it)`, joints into pal, `rx_lbs(pal[..], l)`; corrected rest points `q0[v] = P[v] + sum over targets t with psd_w[t] > 0 of DP[t * P.len + v] * psd_w[t]`; `rx_lbs_from(q0[..], pal[..], q)`; fa = rx_folds of l and fb = rx_folds of q (both with pal, OJ, OW, MK). With `uL = mix_psd_dir(14)` and `uR = mix_psd_dir(18)`, print "pose ", "bind" or `rx_clipname(c)`, " ", rx_pt, " hip tilt ", `atan2(u0.y, u0.x)` in degrees with `u0 = mix_psd_dir(0)`, " L flex ", `atan2(uL.y, uL.x)` in degrees, " abd ", `asin(clamp(uL.z, -1.0, 1.0))` in degrees, " R flex ", the same for uR, " folds ", fa, " -> ", fb, and sum fa and fb over the poses. Print "psd folds (all poses): ", the two sums joined by " -> ". Return TK.len.

`rx_write(d json::Doc&, root int, buf const byte[:], out const byte[:])` writes a copy of the glb with the corrective targets added as glTF morph targets. Let jl = `rx_u32(buf, 12)`, b0 = 20 + jl + 8 and bl = `rx_u32(buf, 20 + jl)` (BIN chunk length). The target meshes are the arguments of `args()` from index 6 on that start with none of "from=", "mush=" and "psd="; argument k is mesh id k - 6 in VM and its vertices are the P entries with that VM, in order. For each, find its index mi in the root's "meshes" array by "name"; skip it with a print when it has no single primitive or that primitive already has "targets". New binary: buf[b0..b0 + bl], padded with zeros to a multiple of 4; then for each target mesh and each target t in order, append the mesh's position deltas (`DP[t * P.len + v]` for its vertices v in order, three little-endian f32 each) and then its normal deltas (DN the same way), and remember for each block its offset, length and, for positions, the componentwise min and max. Emit the JSON with bake's `emit` (used unqualified) for every untouched node, walking objects exactly as emit does: `json::each(d, n) { c => ... }` over member nodes, the key from `json::name_of(d, c)` written with `json::format_key(out, name)`, arrays by `json::count` and `json::element`; numbers go out through `format`-free byte pushes of their decimal text (an int helper and a float helper with up to 7 decimals), rebuilding only: the root's "accessors" array with the old elements followed by one accessor per new block (`{"bufferView":V,"componentType":5126,"count":N,"type":"VEC3"}` plus `"min":[x,y,z],"max":[x,y,z]` for positions), "bufferViews" with the old elements followed by one `{"buffer":0,"byteOffset":O,"byteLength":L}` per new block (V counts from the old view count), "buffers" with element 0's "byteLength" replaced by the new binary length, and in "meshes" each target mesh's object: its members, then "weights" with one 0 per target, then "extras" holding its old members plus "targetNames" (one string per target: "psd:" + the slot's joint node name `gltf::text_of(gltf::nodes[slot_node[TK[t]]].name)` + ":" + TF[t] as a whole number + ":" + TB[t] as a whole number), with its single primitive emitted with an extra "targets" member holding `{"POSITION":A,"NORMAL":A+1}` per target. Pad the JSON with spaces to a multiple of 4. Write "glTF", version 2 and the total length (u32 little-endian each), the JSON chunk (length, 0x4E4F534A, text) and the BIN chunk (length, 0x004E4942, data) to out with `write_file`, and print "psd: wrote ", the target count, " targets on ", the mesh count, " meshes -> ", out.
